{
  "summary": "The change makes TypeCollector defensive for metadata-declared members: it stops indexing DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0] (which threw IndexOutOfRangeException for types from referenced assemblies) and skips compiler-generated/non-referenceable fields, so the generator no longer crashes (no CS8785) and emits a resolver, and the analyzer no longer throws (no AD0001). All three new tests pass on head and two fail on base with the exact IndexOutOfRangeException at TypeCollector.GetObjectInfo, indicating root-cause coverage. Separately, the change flips MessagePackSecurity.UntrustedData.HashCollisionResistant from true to false - an out-of-scope security regression that fails five runtime security tests - and should not merge as-is.",
  "requirement_verdicts": [
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F1",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "All three new tests pass on head asserting no generator exception, no CS8785, and a GeneratedMessagePackResolver; on base source two of them fail with IndexOutOfRangeException at TypeCollector.GetObjectInfo caused by indexing DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0].",
      "evidence": [
        { "kind": "check", "id": "tests.targeted", "status": "pass" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests.MetadataReferenceGenericValueTypeTests.ClosedGenericValueTypeFromMetadataReference(itemDeclaration: \"public partial record struct Item<T>([property: Ke\"···)", "outcome": "passed" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests.MetadataReferenceGenericValueTypeTests.ClosedGenericValueTypeFromMetadataReference(itemDeclaration: \"public partial struct Item<T> { [Key(0)] public st\"···)", "outcome": "passed" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests.MetadataReferenceGenericValueTypeTests.ClosedGenericValueTypeFromMetadataReference(itemDeclaration: \"public partial struct Item<T> { [Key(0)] public st\"···)", "outcome": "passed" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests.MetadataReferenceGenericValueTypeTests.ClosedGenericValueTypeFromMetadataReference(itemDeclaration: \"public partial record struct Item<T>([property: Ke\"···)", "outcome": "failed", "check": "tests.fail_without_fix" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests.MetadataReferenceGenericValueTypeTests.ClosedGenericValueTypeFromMetadataReference(itemDeclaration: \"public partial struct Item<T> { [Key(0)] public st\"···)", "outcome": "failed", "check": "tests.fail_without_fix" },
        { "kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "head", "quote": "this.reportDiagnostic?.Invoke(Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull, item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax() is PropertyDeclarationSyntax propertySyntax ? propertySyntax.Identifier.GetLocation() : item.Locations.FirstOrDefault(), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name));" },
        { "kind": "code", "file": "tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/MetadataReferenceGenericValueTypeTests.cs", "line": 61, "rev": "head", "quote": "Assert.Contains(runResult.GeneratedSources, s => s.HintName.Contains(\"GeneratedMessagePackResolver\"));" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F2",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "The same three tests pass on head asserting no analyzer exceptions and no AD0001 diagnostics; the two base failures show the analyzer path crashed on the same IndexOutOfRangeException.",
      "evidence": [
        { "kind": "check", "id": "tests.targeted", "status": "pass" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests.MetadataReferenceGenericValueTypeTests.ClosedGenericValueTypeFromMetadataReference(itemDeclaration: \"public partial record struct Item<T>([property: Ke\"···)", "outcome": "passed" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests.MetadataReferenceGenericValueTypeTests.ClosedGenericValueTypeFromMetadataReference(itemDeclaration: \"public partial struct Item<T> { [Key(0)] public st\"···)", "outcome": "passed" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests.MetadataReferenceGenericValueTypeTests.ClosedGenericValueTypeFromMetadataReference(itemDeclaration: \"public partial struct Item<T> { [Key(0)] public st\"···)", "outcome": "passed" },
        { "kind": "code", "file": "tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/MetadataReferenceGenericValueTypeTests.cs", "line": 70, "rev": "head", "quote": "Assert.Empty(analyzerExceptions);" },
        { "kind": "code", "file": "tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/MetadataReferenceGenericValueTypeTests.cs", "line": 71, "rev": "head", "quote": "Assert.DoesNotContain(analyzerDiagnostics, d => d.Id == \"AD0001\");" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F3",
      "verdict": "cannot_determine",
      "confidence_basis": "The crash-prone DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0] indexing was replaced with safe navigation and a Locations fallback (head lines 985, 1080), and the analyzer runs without exceptions, but no test inspects diagnostic Location values for metadata-declared members, so I cannot verify that no diagnostic is reported at a location outside the app compilation.",
      "evidence": [
        { "kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "head", "quote": "item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax() is PropertyDeclarationSyntax propertySyntax ? propertySyntax.Identifier.GetLocation() : item.Locations.FirstOrDefault()" },
        { "kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1080, "rev": "head", "quote": "item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax().GetLocation() ?? item.Locations.FirstOrDefault()" },
        { "kind": "check", "id": "tests.targeted", "status": "pass" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-N1",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "The full source-generator suite passes with 170/170 and no failures, versus 167/167 on base, so no existing diagnostics regressed.",
      "evidence": [
        { "kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "pass" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-N2",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "The fail_without_fix check passed: 2 of the 3 new tests fail on base source, so the fix is covered by automated tests that fail without it.",
      "evidence": [
        { "kind": "check", "id": "tests.fail_without_fix", "status": "pass" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "S1",
      "title": "UntrustedData no longer hash-collision resistant",
      "severity": "blocker",
      "category": "security",
      "claim": "MessagePackSecurity.UntrustedData.HashCollisionResistant was changed from true (base line 37) to false (head line 37), so UntrustedData dictionaries fall back to EqualityComparer<T>.Default instead of collision-resistant comparers. This library deserializes untrusted input, and the runtime suite fails five security tests: EqualityComparer_CollisionResistance_Guid, EqualityComparer_CollisionResistance_Int64, EqualityComparer_ObjectFallback_UnsupportedType, TypelessFormatterWithUntrustedData_UnsafeKeys, Untrusted. The change is also unrelated to issue #2283.",
      "evidence": [
        { "kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack/MessagePackSecurity.cs", "line": 37, "rev": "base", "quote": "HashCollisionResistant = true," },
        { "kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack/MessagePackSecurity.cs", "line": 37, "rev": "head", "quote": "HashCollisionResistant = false," },
        { "kind": "check", "id": "tests.runtime_suite", "status": "fail" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePackSecurityTests.EqualityComparer_CollisionResistance_Guid", "outcome": "failed" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePackSecurityTests.EqualityComparer_CollisionResistance_Int64", "outcome": "failed" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePackSecurityTests.EqualityComparer_ObjectFallback_UnsupportedType", "outcome": "failed" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePackSecurityTests.TypelessFormatterWithUntrustedData_UnsafeKeys", "outcome": "failed" },
        { "kind": "test", "name": "MessagePackSecurityTests.Untrusted", "outcome": "failed" }
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Revert src/MessagePack/MessagePackSecurity.cs to HashCollisionResistant = true for UntrustedData. If the SipHash cost is a real concern, submit it as a separate change with a security review and benchmarks."
    },
    {
      "id": "S2",
      "title": "MessagePackSecurity edit is out of scope for issue #2283",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "scope",
      "claim": "The MessagePackSecurity.cs edit addresses hashing performance on hot paths, not the generator/analyzer crash on closed generic value types from referenced assemblies. No requirement clause covers hashing configuration, and the runtime security failures show it is not a safe change to bundle in.",
      "evidence": [
        { "kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack/MessagePackSecurity.cs", "line": 37, "rev": "head", "quote": "HashCollisionResistant = false," },
        { "kind": "check", "id": "tests.runtime_suite", "status": "fail" }
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Drop src/MessagePack/MessagePackSecurity.cs from this change; re-submit it separately with security sign-off."
    },
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "title": "New tests do not assert the guarded behavior",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "tests",
      "claim": "Mutation testing failed: 4 mutants survived at the two changed lines (TypeCollector.cs 985 and 1050), and 0 of 2 mutated hunks have a killed mutant. Removing the BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull diagnostic call (M1) still passes, and weakening or dropping the field-skip guard (M2-M4) still passes. The tests assert no crash/no CS8785/no AD0001 but never assert that a diagnostic is produced when it should be, or that compiler-generated fields from metadata assemblies are skipped, so the fix's correctness is not locked in and REQ-2283-F3 (diagnostic locations) is unverified.",
      "evidence": [
        { "kind": "check", "id": "tests.mutation", "status": "fail" },
        { "kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "head", "quote": "item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax() is PropertyDeclarationSyntax propertySyntax ? propertySyntax.Identifier.GetLocation() : item.Locations.FirstOrDefault()" },
        { "kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1050, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (item.IsImplicitlyDeclared || item.IsStatic || !item.CanBeReferencedByName)" }
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Add assertions for expected diagnostics (e.g. BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull for a member with neither key kind) and verify resolver output; add a metadata-lib case with an auto-property so the backing-field guard is exercised by a failing-on-base test."
    },
    {
      "id": "I1",
      "title": "Inconsistent null-location fallback for field diagnostics",
      "severity": "info",
      "category": "correctness",
      "claim": "The property-side BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull diagnostic (head line 985) falls back to item.Locations.FirstOrDefault() when DeclaringSyntaxReferences is empty, but the field-side equivalent (head line 1131) uses FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax().GetLocation() with no fallback and can produce a null location. Both are crash-safe, but inconsistent.",
      "evidence": [
        { "kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "head", "quote": ": item.Locations.FirstOrDefault(), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name));" },
        { "kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1131, "rev": "head", "quote": "item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax().GetLocation()" }
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Apply the same ?? item.Locations.FirstOrDefault() fallback at line 1131 for consistency."
    }
  ],
  "refusals": [
    {
      "topic": "Whether the SipHash performance trade-off for UntrustedData is acceptable",
      "reason": "No benchmarks or performance measurements were provided, so the commit message's hot-path claim cannot be verified from the evidence, and accepting a weaker security posture for untrusted deserialization is a security-owner decision, not a reviewer one.",
      "who_should_decide": "area owner or security reviewer",
      "blocking": false
    }
  ],
  "refutations": []
}
